senses.gloss:
अभ्य्-अति-√ क्रम् (ind.p. -क्रम्य; Inf. -क्रान्तुं)
to step over, walk through, R.;
to overpower, MBh. xiv, 1551;
to transgress, violate, MBh. i, 199.

1. अभ्य्-अनु-√ ज्ञा to assent to, approve, allow, permit, concede, MBh. &c.;
to authorize, direct, MBh. ii, 1225;
to allow one to depart, dismiss, MBh. &c.;
 (ind.p. -ज्ञाय; Inf. -ज्ञातुम्)
to take leave, ask for leave to depart, MBh. xiv, 146; R. :
Caus. (ind.p. -ज्ञाप्य; fut. p. -ज्ञापयिष्यत्)
to ask for leave to depart, MBh.

अभ्य्-√ अर्च् (3. pl. -अर्चन्ति and impf. -अर्चन् [RV. iv, 1, 14]; Imper. 2. sg. -अर्च, 2. pl. -अर्चत; Ā. 1. sg. -अर्चे and aor. -अर्चसे [RV. x, 64, 3])
to praise, celebrate in song (instr.), RV.; AV.; VS.;
 (ind.p. -अर्च्य) to worship, reverence, MBh.; Mn. &c.

अभ्य्-√ अर्थ् Ā. (Opt. 2. sg. -अर्थयेथास्; rarely P., e.g. fut. -अर्थयिष्यति, Kathās.)
to request, ask for (acc. or dat. or loc. or in comp. with अर्थम्), MBh. iii, 16990, &c.;
 (see also अभ्य्-√ अर्त्.)

अभ्य्-√ अर्ष् (Imper. 2. sg. -अर्षा or -अर्ष (most frequently in RV.); p. -अ॑र्षत्)
to flow or run near (acc.), RV.;
to cause to flow near, afford, RV.;
 (aor. or plusq. -आनर्षत्), TĀr.

अभ्य्-अव-√ निज् P. -नेनेक्ति, to wipe or wash, clean, Kauś.;
 (aor. Ā. 1. sg. -निक्षि), AV. x, 5, 15:
Caus. to cause to wash, Kauś.

अभ्य्-अव-√ सृज् (1. p. -सृजामि) to dismiss towards (acc.), AV. xvi, 1, 6;
to dismiss (as rays), MBh. xii, 3295;
to throw, shoot (as arrows), MBh.; R.

अभ्य्-अव-√ हृ to throw down into water (acc.; अपः॑ or समुद्र॑म् or ह्रद॑म्), VS.; ŚBr.; ĀśvŚr. (cf. अभ्य्-अव-√ नी);
to bring near, ŚBr.;
to take food, eat, Suśr.; Car. &c.:
Caus. to cause to throw down (into water), Lāṭy.;
to attack (as an enemy), MBh. iii, 16369;
to take food, eat, MBh. iii, 15905;
to cause to eat, Daś.

अभ्य्-अवे (√ इ), -अवैति to go down, descend (into water, as in bathing), AitBr.; ŚBr.; KātyŚr.;
 (fut. 3. pl. -अवैष्यन्ति) to condescend, ŚBr.;
 (impf. 3. pl. -अवा॑यन्) to perceive, TS.

अभ्य्-√ 1. अश् -अश्नोति, (frequently Opt. or Prec. 1. sg. -अश्याम्, 3. sg. -अश्यास् [RV. iv, 5, 7], 1. pl. -अश्याम; aor. P. -आनट् and Ā. -आ॑ष्ट; perf. 1. pl. -आनश्म, 3. pl. -आनशुः॑)
to pervade, reach to, gain, RV.;
 (Subj. 1. du. -अश्न॑वाव, 1. pl. -अश्न॑वाम) to overpower, RV.

1. अभ्य्-√ 1. अस् -अ॑स्ति (1. pl. अभि॑ष्मस्, but 3. pl. अभि॑ स॑न्ति and pr. p. अभि॑ स॑त् [according to Pāṇ. viii, 3, 87 अभिस्मस्, but अभिषन्ति and अभिषत्]; Subj. -असत्, 1. pl. -अ॑साम, 3. pl. -अ॑सन्; Pot. sg. -ष्याम्, -ष्यास्, -ष्यात्, 1. and 3. pl. -ष्याम, -ष्युः or -ष्युः॑; perf. 1. sg. -आस)
to be over, reign over, excel, surpass, overpower, RV.; AV.;
to fall to one's share, Pāṇ. i, 4, 91.

2. अभ्य्-√ 2. अस् (ind.p. -अस्य) to throw towards or upon, ŚBr.; AitBr.;
 (p. gen. sg. -अस्यतस्) to throw (as arrows), MBh. i, 5479;
to add, Śulb.: P. (rarely Ā.) -अस्यति (but also Pot. -असेत्, Mn.; p. -असत्, MBh. iii, 1450; R.; Yājñ. iii, 204 :
Ā. -असते, Mn. iv, 149) to concentrate one's attention upon (acc.), practise, exercise, study, MBh. &c.;
to repeat, double;
to multiply, Sūryas. &c.:
Caus. to cause to practise or study, teach Comm. on Śiś. ix, 79.

अभ्य्-आश, अस्, m. (also written 1. अभ्य्-आस), reaching to, pervading, Yājñ. iii, 114;
 (with यद् and Pot.) prospect, any expected result or consequence, ChUp.;
 proximity (with gen. or abl.), R. &c.;
 (mfn.) near, Kum. vi, 2;
 (अम्), ind. near, at hand, AitBr.; PBr.;
 (ए), loc. ind. near (with gen. or abl.), R. &c.;
 (आत्), abl. in comp. with (a perf. Pass. p., as) आगत, &c., arrived from near at hand, &c., Pāṇ. ii, 1, 39, Sch. & vi, 3, 2, Sch..

