अभ्य्-आ-√ 1. गा (aor. अभ्य्-आ॑गात्) to approach, come to (acc.), RV. i, 164, 27; MBh.;
 (gen.), BhP.;
 (said of evil) to visit, MBh. iii, 1120;
to begin to (Inf.), Mn. x, 108.

अभ्य्-आ-√ 1. दा Ā. (rarely P. Hariv.) to seize, snatch away, (Pot. -ददीत), MBh. i, 3558 = xii, 10999 = xiii, 4985 :
Ā. to put on (as a wreath), Hariv.;
 (with वाक्यम्) to take up the word, commence to speak, MBh. v, 3384.

अभ्य्-आ-√ यम् P. (3. pl. -यच्छन्ति) to lengthen (as a syllable in speaking), AitBr.;
to draw or pull (as the udder in sucking), Kāṭh. : Ā. (Imper. 2. sg. -यच्छस्व) to assume (‘to grant’ Comm.), VS. iii, 38 : P. (Subj. 3. pl. -यमन्; ind.p. -य॑त्य)
to aim at, RV. viii, 92, 31; ŚBr.; AitBr.;
 for अभ्य्-आ-√ गम्, KauṣBr.

अभ्य्-आ-√ हन् (Imper. 2. sg. -जहि॑; perf. Ā. -जघ्ने)
to strike, wound, RV. ix, 85, 2; MBh.; ChUp.;
to impede (Inf. -हनितुम्), Hariv.

अभ्य्-उत्-था (√ स्था), (impf. -उ॑दतिष्ठत्; perf. -उ॑त्-तस्थौ)
to rise for going towards (acc.), AV. xv, 8, 5; ŚBr. &c.;
to rise from a seat to do any one (acc.) honour, Śāk. &c.;
 (with आतिथ्य-कर्म) id., MBh. viii, 634;
to rise in rebellion, MārkP.;
to leave off, desist from (abl.) Comm. on ChUp.

अभ्य्-उद्-√ इ (2. sg. -एषि; Imper. 2. sg. -उ॑द्-इहि; Pot. -इयात् [ŚBr.], -ईयात् [MBh. iii, 2010 and 10272]; fut. -उद्-अयिष्यति, MBh. iv, 688), (said of the sun)
to rise over (acc.), rise, RV. viii, 93, 1; AV. &c.;
to engage in combat with (acc.), MBh. (Pot. -ईयात् See before);
to finish off at (acc.), PBr.

अभ्य्-उद्-धृ (√ हृ), Ved. to take out (especially one fire in order to add it to another), TS.; ŚBr. &c.;
to take or draw out, draw (as water), MBh. &c.;
to take up, lift up, ŚāṅkhŚr.; MBh. xii, 12322;
to re-obtain, Yājñ. ii, 119;
to elevate, render prosperous, MBh.; Sāh. &c.:
Caus. (ind.p. -उद्धार्य) to raise, lift up, MBh. iii, 13326.

अभ्य्-उप-√ गम् to go near to, approach, arrive at (acc.), MBh. &c.;
to obtain;
to assent, agree to, Daś. &c.:
Caus. (ind.p. -गमय्य) to prevail on any one to assent, Daś. (see also अभ्य्-उपगमित).

अभ्य्-उप-√ पद् Ā. -पद्यते, to approach in order to help, MBh. &c.;
to ask for help, R. iii, 14, 7;
to furnish with, MBh. ii, 187.

1. अभ्य्-उपे (√ इ), -उपैति (3. pl. -उ॑पयन्ति) to go near, approach, arrive at, enter, RV. vi, 28, 4; ŚBr. &c.;
 (with अपः) to bathe, KātyŚr.; Mn. xi, 259; Yājñ.;
to approach (in copulation), Hit.;
to go to meet any one (acc.), BhP.;
to enter a state or condition, obtain, share, AitBr. (Ved. Inf. -उपैतोस्), MBh. &c.;
to admit as an argument or a position, RPrāt. (perf. p. gen. pl. -उपेयुषाम्) Comm. on Nyāyam. and on Bād.;
to select as (acc.), MBh. i, 811;
to agree with, approve of Daś. (see अभ्य्-उपेत) :
Pass. -उपेयते to be approved of, admitted, Sarvad.
